  "details": "VRChat have a very unclear way to handle disconnects, that most of the time don't look to try to reconnect without reloading the entire instance. Would be better to instead of erroring out and giving a misleading \"continue\" button that's actually a reconnect button, would. Be better to \"freeze\" the player and show a countdown timer (or something more clever) where the client tries to reconnect without reloading, that would be less jarring and less misleading because the \"VRChat is not working\" error reads wrongfully, and I think that giving atleast better error messages would be already nicer for people. And less jarring too than disconnecting and needing to reload the e entire thing.\n\nMake the client more resilient to disconnects and not lose track of you locally and try to resync it.",
